WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.930
<b>Pirate Zoro vs. Priest Ohm</b>

3
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.180
[OHM]
Quite the gathering.

4
00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.930
How many players remain
in our little game?

5
00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.310
We have four
Divine Squad members.

6
00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.310
And since I doubt the wounds
I dealt those two were fatal,

7
00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.060
that leaves us with
four Shandorians

8
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.610
and one Blue Sea dweller.

9
00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.650
Counting the Lord
of the Sky and Holy,

10
00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.910
that's ten people
and two animals.

11
00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.910
just as God Eneru predicted.
So, there we stand.

12
00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.330
...for harming Wyper!

13
00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.750
Is that so?

14
00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.170
You'd willingly forfeit
your life for this sad speck?

15
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.590
Mind who you throw
your loyalty to, savage!

16
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.920
You cannot run!

17
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.920
Enough of this... Holy,
it's time for your Mad Dash.

18
00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.490
Huh?!

19
00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.710
[yelling]

20
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.000
[groaning]

21
00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.300
[gasps, screams]

22
00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.010
Don't stop! Finish it!

23
00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.150
[gasps]

24
00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.900
He's building some
kind of fence.

25
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.320
Damn.

26
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.660
He's using more of his tricks.
This could be trouble.

27
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.620
[grunts]
No tricks here!

28
00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:28.920
Behold, the Ordeal of Iron!

29
00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.090
[DIVINE SQUAD A]
The White
Barbed Death Match has begun!

30
00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.630
So, you can put up a fence.

31
00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:40.250
Big deal. I wasn't
planning to run.

32
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.250
[bleats]

33
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.210
The purpose of this barrier
isn't just to hold you.

34
00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.960
Yes, there's a reason
it's called White Barbs.

35
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:48.840
What's that?

36
00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.140
[WYPER]
Huh?

37
00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.430
[WYPER]
Show us!

38
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.520
[groaning]

39
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.990
I guess the thorns are painful.
Thanks for the warning.

40
00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.970
So how do I get outta here
once I'm done with all'a you?

41
00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:08.560
You can worry about that later,
assuming you survive.

42
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.230
[OHM]
Only eight people
and two animals left.

43
00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:20.320
[LAKI]
Wyper...

44
00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.310
[LAKI gasps]

45
00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.640
[LAKI]
Wyper!

46
00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.560
Wyper! Listen!

47
00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.600
Laki!

48
00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:31.690
Quickly! There isn't much time!

49
00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.110
What's wrong?
Why are you here?

50
00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:39.660
I had to come to give you
Kamakiri's warning!

51
00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.950
Nobody can beat... Eneru...

52
00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.060
You must run away!

53
00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.620
Abandon this fight!

54
00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:48.670
[WYPER grunts]

55
00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.670
[LAKI panting]

56
00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.820
Eneru. He's in the forest.

57
00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:00.990
Enough!

58
00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:06.280
Eneru is lightning itself. He
truly has the powers of a God!

59
00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.950
Stop!

60
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.540
Leave! At once!

61
00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.370
He cannot be defeated!

62
00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.080
[WYPER]
Do as I say!

63
00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.070
Did I hear my name?

64
00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.210
Eneru.

65
00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:29.460
Eneru!

66
00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.040
Leave her be!

67
00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.170
Laki's not here to fight!

68
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.050
I'm the one you want!

69
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.130
Laki! Run!

70
00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.760
You're a fool!

71
00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:41.510
I'd forget about her and
worry more about myself!

72
00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.640
[grunts]

73
00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.430
[growling]

74
00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.690
[panting]

75
00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.980
[KAMAKIRI]
Laki... Hear me.

76
00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.420
and rightly so.

77
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.590
He can't be conquered.

78
00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.090
[growling]

79
00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:06.970
[DIVINE SQUAD A grunts]

80
00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.050
You've sealed your fate, Wyper!

81
00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.930
Huh?

82
00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.060
You damn fool.

83
00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.490
Please survive.

84
00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.450
[LAKI sighs]

85
00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:41.300
[ENERU laughing]

86
00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.470
[WYPER growling]
Eneru!

87
00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.430
Huh? You should be
writhing in pure agony.

88
00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.180
Let's try that again!

89
00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.600
[grunts, groans]

90
00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:02.700
You didn't actually
think I'd spare her?

91
00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.700
Wyper, the "ruthless
Shandorian warrior."

92
00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.580
Surely you understand
the concept of "no mercy"?

93
00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.040
She opposed me,
and now she's dead.

94
00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.790
You'll join her soon enough.

95
00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:23.130
[ENERU laughing]

96
00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.810
[DIVINE SQUAD C grunts]

97
00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.640
[SHANDORIAN B yelling]

98
00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:38.900
That's him?

99
00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:40.230
That's God?

100
00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.860
Weep not for her.

101
00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.510
that all God's children
pray for. She is free.

102
00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:44.930
Since we're all
gettin' personal,

103
00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:48.600
there's a score I
have to settle as well.

104
00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:49.980
[WYPER, ZORO]
– The snake!
– The snake!

105
00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.560
Time to cough up
what's in your belly!

106
00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.790
[WYPER growls]
Get out of my way!

107
00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.360
[ZORO, WYPER grunt]

108
00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.320
Holy! They need a hug!

109
00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.950
[HOLY roars]

110
00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.540
[OHM]
Eisen Whip!

111
00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:05.750
[ZORO gasps]

112
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.250
Axe Dial!

113
00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:12.170
[groaning]

114
00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.770
The numbers dwindle.

115
00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.600
Six people and
two animals remain.

116
00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:34.150
[roars]

117
00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.620
Good sign.

118
00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:39.630
By the looks of it, I'd say
she wasn't seriously injured.

119
00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:43.250
[GAN FALL grunting]

120
00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:44.390
Where in the world
is this place?

121
00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.770
We got swallowed up, remember?

122
00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.690
Ah, yes. Of course.

123
00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.360
The beast seems even
larger from the inside.

124
00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:52.440
[AISA grunting]

125
00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:53.860
[NAMI]
Aisa, are you okay?

126
00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:55.030
[gasps]

127
00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:58.200
Wyper, please forgive me!

128
00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.090
[gasping]

129
00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.550
Pierre!

130
00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.560
[AISA]
What happened?

131
00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:06.760
[NAMI]
Right, for the umpteenth time...

132
00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:09.350
We've been eaten by a snake.

133
00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:10.490
A snake?!

134
00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.320
[NAMI]
Calm down. We'll survive.

135
00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:15.840
If we can escape
before it digests us.

136
00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.560
What were you two
doing out there?

137
00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.510
You should be on the ship.

138
00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.630
Tell that to the creeps
who were chasing us.

139
00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:23.870
We had to run for lives.

140
00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:26.070
Isn't that little
girl a Shandorian?

141
00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:27.900
[whimpering]

142
00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.320
Gan Fall, it's you!

143
00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.910
[yelling]
I'll mash
you into pieces!

144
00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.490
Stop. Just calm down.

145
00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:38.750
Anyway, why don't we
simply carve our way out?

146
00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.370
Are you insane, old man?!

147
00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:42.630
Suppose the snake
starts going wild!

148
00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.420
You're gonna get us all killed!

149
00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.460
Ya know, for a knight,
you're pretty dense!

150
00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.160
I, uh, was kidding.

151
00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.790
Take a look around you!
We are in a stomach!

152
00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.540
A snake's stomach!

153
00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.420
I don't know how much
you know about anatomy,

154
00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:55.300
but it won't be long
before we're bathing

155
00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.510
in its metabolic acid!

156
00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:00.140
[BOTH gasp]

157
00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:01.730
[cries]

158
00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.610
Nami! Weird knight guy!

159
00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:06.230
It's you.

160
00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:07.940
Luffy...

161
00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:10.490
[LUFFY]
I was starting to think
I was the only one here.

162
00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:12.280
Isn't this the strangest cave?

163
00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.710
[PIERRE chirps]

164
00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.130
Huh. That's an understatement.
How'd you end up here?

165
00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.340
I don't know.

166
00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.680
I just got stuck here
and I can't get out.

167
00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.180
Incredible.

168
00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.920
This snake's turning out
to be a serious problem.

169
00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.400
Uh! A snake?

170
00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.590
Who'd you think this
stomach belonged to?

171
00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:33.180
But... How could you
be here talking to me

172
00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.970
if you were swallowed
by a giant snake?

173
00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:38.230
Like I said!

174
00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.690
Big, blue reptile
with mile-long fangs!

175
00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:43.770
It ate us and now we're
stuck in its belly!

176
00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:47.030
Ow, come on, Nami. That hurts!

177
00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:50.610
Heh! Hi, I'm Usopp!

178
00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:51.950
[LUFFY laughs]

179
00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:54.850
Is he a... jester?

180
00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.810
That job would suit him best

181
00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:59.230
but he's actually Captain.

182
00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:00.860
[gasping]

183
00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:02.230
He's your captain?

184
00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.110
My word.

185
00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.840
What's this world coming to?

186
00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:09.880
You sure are calm for someone
who's been eaten by a monster.

187
00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:11.300
[screams]

188
00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.010
Wait a minute! I thought that
Nami was only joking!

189
00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:16.060
You mean we're being
eaten by a snake?!

190
00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:18.060
I've been trying to tell you...

191
00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:20.350
Its stomach acid is
melting your clothes.

192
00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.310
[gasping]

193
00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.120
Whoa, you're right!

194
00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:25.670
Well, what're we waitin' for?

195
00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.600
We need to find its
butthole right away!

196
00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.640
Ridiculous.

197
00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:31.560
You're despicable!

198
00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.020
Why? Maybe we can get out

199
00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.020
next time the snake
goes to the bathroom.

200
00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:39.070
No! I'd rather get digested!

201
00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.260
Nami's scary.

202
00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.780
I know what you mean, child.
She's meaner than the snake.

203
00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:45.110
[sighs]

204
00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:47.240
Hardly. When the snake
gets in a bad mood

205
00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:48.610
it starts eating people.

206
00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:51.030
And speaking of which,
we'd better think fast.

207
00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:53.240
Its temper was wild enough
on the outside, and be...

208
00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.780
[LUFFY]
Wait, the snake was
in a "bad mood"?

209
00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.290
[ALL gasp]

210
00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.540
[LUFFY]
Hm?

211
00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.210
[NAMI]
Luffy. What have
you been doing in here?

212
00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.630
Oh. I was tryin' to
bust through a wall.

213
00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:07.880
Didn't work, though.

214
00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.930
[laughing]

215
00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.760
Ah, so this is all your doing.

216
00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:15.510
Throwing all those punches
burned up a lot of energy.

217
00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:19.730
Say, um... Did any of you
think to bring some food?

218
00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.390
What's wrong?

219
00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:26.410
How about you eat my fist!

220
00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:32.160
[growling]

221
00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:36.670
[ALL gasping]

222
00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:42.920
[ALL screaming]

223
00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:50.850
[roars]

224
00:12:58.100 --> 00:12:59.310
Heh.

225
00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.570
What's the matter,
gotta belly ache?

226
00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.280
It serves ya right!

227
00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:10.070
[SNAKE growls]

228
00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:13.450
[WYPER]
It won't be long, Aisa! Hold on!

229
00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:18.870
[WYPER]
Open up, serpent!

230
00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.170
[ZORO panting]

231
00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.040
[ZORO]
This is getting really old.

232
00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:46.340
That extendable sword
he's using is a pain.

233
00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:47.840
And that snake...

234
00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.670
I already know defeating him
first isn't exactly gonna be

235
00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:50.840
a walk in the park.

236
00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.460
But I have to get Nami
and the old Knight

237
00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.290
out of that thing's
gut right now.

238
00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.450
There's still time. Since
they were swallowed whole,

239
00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.540
I would bet they're
not dead yet.

240
00:13:58.620 --> 00:13:59.710
[SNAKE roaring]

241
00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:02.460
[ZORO]
But it won't be
that way for long.

242
00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.300
[OHM]
Eisen Whip!

243
00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.120
Not again!

244
00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:14.140
[ZORO grunts]

245
00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.690
That bastard. Where is he?

246
00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:25.610
[OHM]
Eisen Whip!

247
00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:05.990
You're dead!

248
00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:08.030
Make that four people.

249
00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:11.580
[SHANDORIAN A groaning]

250
00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.600
[ZORO]
Two Swords Style!

251
00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.000
[OHM grunts]

252
00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.170
Hawk Wave!

253
00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.580
Eisen Back Wall!

254
00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.860
[ZORO grunting]

255
00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.860
[ZORO]
An iron wall...?

256
00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:26.320
[OHM]
This sword is an iron cloud.

257
00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:34.250
[OHM]
You didn't think clouds
had a set shape did you?

258
00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.270
You!

259
00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.840
Eisen Fan!

260
00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:41.090
Eisen Fork!

261
00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.370
[ZORO yelps]

262
00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.710
Eisen Rapier! Ha!

263
00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.670
[groans]

264
00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.550
[ZORO]
He's predicting my movements.

265
00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.850
Why can't I avoid it?

266
00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.310
What's the matter?

267
00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.720
Keeping your distance
doesn't do you any good

268
00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.520
when you depend on your sword.

269
00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.440
[ZORO]
You're wrong about that.

270
00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.020
Huh?

271
00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.440
[growls]

272
00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:12.360
Thirty-six Caliber Phoenix!

273
00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:15.040
Eisen Whip!

274
00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.790
[ZORO]
How could he block it?

275
00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:23.880
[OHM grunts]

276
00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.790
[ZORO grunting]

277
00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.300
[ZORO grunts]

278
00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:34.390
[ZORO]
Dammit!

279
00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.800
[OHM]
That's quite an
interesting technique

280
00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:41.430
you've developed,
Blue Sea Dweller.

281
00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:47.770
[OHM]
I wonder if
you'll try that again.

282
00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:52.190
Unfortunately, even if
you lose sight of me,

283
00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:54.280
I'll always know
where you are...

284
00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.400
[ZORO panting]

285
00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:59.460
...by using Mantora.

286
00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:12.660
[OHM]
Looks like we just
lost another one.

287
00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:16.410
Now there are two animals
and three people left.

288
00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.560
[OHM]
But soon there
will be two animals

289
00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:25.100
and only two people.

290
00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:28.850
[SNAKE roars]

291
00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:33.490
[OHM]
So you're the leader of
the Blue Sea People up here.

292
00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:38.950
You and your comrades
all put up a good fight.

293
00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:42.930
However, my sword is now
pointed directly at your heart.

294
00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:46.680
[OHM]
Say your prayers, swordsman!

295
00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.690
[ZORO]
Don't be an idiot.

296
00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:52.150
I never pray for anything.

297
00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:53.480
[OHM]
That's too bad.

298
00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.010
You should use your resources.

299
00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:57.530
I don't have to see you.

300
00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:59.570
I can follow that
extendable sword of yours

301
00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:01.950
and know exactly where you are!

302
00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.310
[OHM]
Hmph. Well, the moment
you find me, you die!

303
00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:09.580
One life holds 36
worldly desires.

304
00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:12.620
[ZORO]
Two lives hold 72.

305
00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:16.460
Three lives hold
108 worldly desires.

306
00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:23.550
Three swords...
108 Caliber Phoenix!

307
00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:29.310
[OHM]
He broke
through the iron clouds!

308
00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.660
[ZORO]
...huh?!

309
00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.000
You mean this dog
obeys anyone?

310
00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.310
[barks]

311
00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:06.730
[sighs]

312
00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:07.690
In that case, just knock
yourself unconscious.

313
00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:08.390
That's just it, they're not bad.

314
00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:19.350
[ROBIN]
Shandora. The City of Gold.

315
00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:21.390
And if the golden bell
said to be in the middle

316
00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:24.940
of the city isn't here,
where is it?

317
00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:28.690
The belfry was probably
engraved with poneglyphs.

318
00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.570
[ROBIN]
If that's the case,
then the city probably fell

319
00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.950
in order to protect them.

320
00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:40.330
[ROBIN]
Even after all this time,

321
00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:43.960
the belfry and the poneglyphs
should still be here.

322
00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.410
They're hidden somewhere.

323
00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.540
Hey, what's that?

324
00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:55.550
A rail used to run
through this city.

325
00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.970
[ROBIN]
But this is new.

326
00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:02.230
Something was moved out of here.

327
00:20:02.310 --> 00:20:04.350
I wonder what it was.

328
00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:08.730
[ENERU laughs]
Isn't it amazing?

329
00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:12.650
Even after being shot up into
the sky, the city of Shandora

330
00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:15.030
still majestically
exists in this way.

331
00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:20.060
[ENERU laughs]
Even if it's a
city that everyone knows about,

332
00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:21.860
how can it show off
its lovely figure

333
00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:25.580
if it's covered by clouds?

334
00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.660
[ENERU]
I'm the only one
who could see it.

335
00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:33.520
I discovered it. The former
Gods never even noticed.

336
00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.170
And who are you?

337
00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.630
I'm God.

338
00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:43.740
[ENERU]
You're quite intelligent.

339
00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.450
One might guess that you're an
archeologist from the Blue Sea

340
00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:49.580
world by how fast you
found this city of ruins.

341
00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:52.700
It took us several months
to find the same thing.

342
00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.910
I suppose it's easier if
you can read the letters

343
00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:57.240
on the ruins, right?

344
00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:03.370
Unfortunately, the gold you're
looking for isn't here anymore.

345
00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.000
I'm afraid you're a few
years too late for that.

346
00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.360
The gold?

347
00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:09.590
Well, you're right about that.
I couldn't find any.

348
00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.580
You must've been
the one who removed it.

349
00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:14.620
[ENERU]
Gold is a wonderful
thing to have and

350
00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:18.910
that glittering metal suits
me well, don't you think?

351
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:21.120
[ROBIN]
Then you must also
have taken the golden bell

352
00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:22.220
that was once here.

353
00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:24.720
[ENERU]
Hm? There was a golden bell?

354
00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:26.890
[ROBIN gasps]
He doesn't know!

355
00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:37.070
Well I'm very intrigued.

356
00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:41.150
What did you learn by reading
those letters on the bell?

357
00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.490
[ROBIN]
Actually, it's too bad,
I never got to read them.

358
00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:49.280
If you say it wasn't here when
you arrived, it must not exist.

359
00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:51.920
I guess the huge golden
bell and belfry that were

360
00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:55.050
the pride of Shandora must have
only been another legend.

361
00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:59.040
It's a shame that I'll never be
able to lay my eyes on them.

362
00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.120
No, wait.

363
00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:02.670
It's... It's actually
right here.

364
00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:04.710
It's here in the sky!

365
00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:08.010
When this island was blown
into the sky 400 years ago

366
00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:10.840
and the Upper Yard was born...

367
00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:13.180
Or, when "Godland" was born,

368
00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:15.390
it was said that the
loud chimes of a bell

369
00:22:15.470 --> 00:22:18.520
could be heard ringing
throughout the entire nation.

370
00:22:22.250 --> 00:22:24.000
[ENERU]
The elder
inhabitants of this land

371
00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:26.580
called it the island's
singing voice.

372
00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:28.170
But that wasn't it.

373
00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:29.630
It was the bell!

374
00:22:29.710 --> 00:22:31.710
The bell made of gold!

375
00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:32.760
Amazing!

376
00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:34.800
Soon the entire game
will be over.

377
00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.760
Only eight minutes left.

378
00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:38.600
That's not long at all. In fact,

379
00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:42.440
it gives me plenty of time
to look for the golden bell.

380
00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:46.900
[ENERU chuckles]

381
00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:49.530
[ROBIN]
So the golden
bell is in the sky?

382
00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:51.860
Which means the
poneglyphs are, too!

383
00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:53.410
[laughing]

384
00:22:53.490 --> 00:22:54.780
Hm?

385
00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:56.780
[MAN A panting]

386
00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:58.080
Interesting.

387
00:22:58.160 --> 00:23:01.660
It sounds like there's
a maggot on the island.

388
00:23:02.680 --> 00:23:04.760
Thank you, Father.

389
00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:08.470
[SUU]
Suu!

390
00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:11.980
Suu! Suu! Suu!

391
00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:13.440
[PAGAYA]
What's the matter with you, Suu?

392
00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:15.020
Did we forget to feed you?

393
00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:17.770
Oh, Suu, are you in pain?
Or did something happen?

394
00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:19.400
[SUU chirping]

395
00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:21.070
[MAN A groans]

396
00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:26.530
[PAGAYA]
Are... Are you...?

397
00:23:26.620 --> 00:23:28.530
[MAN A]
Yes, I'm one of the men

398
00:23:28.690 --> 00:23:31.510
who used to serve Gan Fall
when he was God.

399
00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:33.770
[PAGAYA]
So you're one of
the Divine Warriors!

400
00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:40.150
[MAN A groans]
We were in a
closed off area, and then...

401
00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:42.480
[PAGAYA]
Goodness, what on
earth happened to you?

402
00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:44.100
Conis, he needs
your help right away!

403
00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:45.450
Yes, of course father!

404
00:23:46.090 --> 00:23:48.150
[MAN A]
No wait!

405
00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:50.150
My family's on Angel Island.

406
00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:52.070
Please... Please help.

407
00:23:52.150 --> 00:23:53.320
[PAGAYA]
I will.

408
00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:55.160
I know everyone's worried
about all of you.

409
00:23:55.240 --> 00:24:00.370
Let everyone know Eneru... he's
planning to return everything!

410
00:24:00.520 --> 00:24:02.020
[PAGAYA]
What?

411
00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:04.230
[MAN A]
Skypiea will be dropped
back into the Blue Sea world,

412
00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:07.250
and this entire nation
will no longer exist!

413
00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:10.400
But that... can't be true!

414
00:24:10.480 --> 00:24:13.280
[CONIS gasping]

415
00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:16.080
There's no time to lose.
You must tell everyone.

416
00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:18.280
Do it, now!

417
00:24:19.210 --> 00:24:20.840
[MAN A]
Our lives will soon be over.

418
00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:23.260
Eneru is planning to eliminate
every living person

419
00:24:23.340 --> 00:24:25.260
from the sky!

420
00:24:27.890 --> 00:24:30.010
Eliminate everyone from the sky?

421
00:24:30.100 --> 00:24:33.340
But wait... If he succeeds
in that then...

422
00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.090
...he won't have
a place to live.

423
00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:37.780
It doesn't make any sense.
Why would he want to do that?

424
00:24:37.860 --> 00:24:39.570
He built a ship.

425
00:24:39.750 --> 00:24:41.170
The Ark Maxim.

426
00:24:42.090 --> 00:24:44.460
[PAGAYA]
Ark Maxim...?

427
00:24:45.540 --> 00:24:47.540
Hey, what are y...?

428
00:24:47.620 --> 00:24:49.250
[gasps]

429
00:24:55.740 --> 00:24:57.030
We were forced to spend

430
00:24:57.270 --> 00:24:59.900
the last six years of our lives
building that ship!

431
00:24:59.980 --> 00:25:00.730
[CONIS yelps]

432
00:25:00.820 --> 00:25:02.030
[gasping]

433
00:25:08.240 --> 00:25:10.580
Father!

434
00:25:10.660 --> 00:25:12.790
When the sky finally
becomes peaceful,

435
00:25:12.870 --> 00:25:15.910
I'd like to be able to show
everyone the hospitality

436
00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.670
they once knew to
my heart's content.

437
00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:20.630
Including you.

438
00:25:37.430 --> 00:25:39.430
[gasps]
What exactly
did you just do?

439
00:25:41.190 --> 00:25:42.350
I showed mercy.

440
00:25:43.160 --> 00:25:47.450
[ROBIN]
This man, he has Logia Power!

441
00:25:47.540 --> 00:25:50.540
And now, I must say that what
little time we have left here

442
00:25:50.620 --> 00:25:52.170
is coming to a close.

443
00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:54.250
This is the beginning
of the end.

444
00:25:54.340 --> 00:25:56.840
I will now set into motion
a series of events

445
00:25:56.920 --> 00:25:59.420
that will reveal
my ultimate plan.

446
00:25:59.480 --> 00:26:02.480
What plan? What do you mean?

447
00:26:04.790 --> 00:26:06.750
[ENERU]
The Sky Lord is calling to you!

448
00:26:06.960 --> 00:26:11.000
Heed my call, lowly
beings, and come to me!

449
00:26:12.170 --> 00:26:13.590
[ROBIN gasps]

450
00:26:15.850 --> 00:26:17.260
[ENERU]
Sango!

451
00:26:24.270 --> 00:26:25.060
What the...?

452
00:26:37.620 --> 00:26:38.910
What are you doing?

453
00:26:39.290 --> 00:26:41.000
[ENERU laughs]

454
00:26:41.080 --> 00:26:42.870
[ENERU]
It was I who brought you

455
00:26:42.960 --> 00:26:45.420
and your friends
here to Shandora.

456
00:26:45.500 --> 00:26:47.630
I beckoned you.

457
00:26:48.250 --> 00:26:50.630
[ROBIN]
I've never seen
anything like this before.

458
00:26:50.710 --> 00:26:53.880
This man possesses
such tremendous power.

459
00:27:00.890 --> 00:27:02.560
The whole place
is falling apart.

460
00:27:05.960 --> 00:27:07.250
[WYPER]
It's Eneru!

461
00:27:07.340 --> 00:27:08.960
He's the only one
who's powerful enough

462
00:27:09.050 --> 00:27:11.050
to do something like this.

463
00:27:13.550 --> 00:27:16.260
I better think of something.

464
00:27:17.070 --> 00:27:18.200
[gasps]
Chopper!

465
00:27:20.350 --> 00:27:22.440
[ZORO yelling, gasps]

466
00:27:24.440 --> 00:27:25.560
[ZORO grunts]

467
00:27:26.230 --> 00:27:27.900
[ZORO groans]

468
00:27:31.650 --> 00:27:34.990
What's that...?
There's a hole at the base.

469
00:27:42.120 --> 00:27:44.580
[ENERU laughing]

470
00:27:44.670 --> 00:27:48.290
And now this brings us
to our climactic finale.

471
00:27:50.620 --> 00:27:52.830
[GAN FALL]
I suggest we
attempt our escape now.

472
00:27:52.920 --> 00:27:55.380
Right. Yeah.
It's now or never.

473
00:27:55.460 --> 00:27:57.590
Luffy get over here and
grab hold of the waver.

474
00:27:57.670 --> 00:27:59.960
I'm gonna finally get
us out of this snake.

475
00:28:00.050 --> 00:28:02.350
Right. Hey, you, hang on to me.

476
00:28:02.370 --> 00:28:03.910
Here we go!

477
00:28:03.930 --> 00:28:05.680
[engine revs]

478
00:28:05.770 --> 00:28:08.390
Yay. Can't wait to get out.

479
00:28:08.480 --> 00:28:09.690
[AISA, LUFFY yelp]

480
00:28:09.770 --> 00:28:12.560
[GAN FALL]
Man overboard!
We can't leave them!

481
00:28:12.650 --> 00:28:16.190
Pierre, go back! You have
to save those two!

482
00:28:16.280 --> 00:28:17.690
[GAN FALL screams]

483
00:28:17.780 --> 00:28:19.240
[PIERRE squawks]

484
00:28:19.320 --> 00:28:21.740
[NAMI screams]

485
00:28:21.820 --> 00:28:23.240
[NAMI gasps]

486
00:28:24.870 --> 00:28:28.160
[NAMI gasping]

487
00:28:28.250 --> 00:28:29.920
How'd we get so high up?

488
00:28:30.010 --> 00:28:32.680
[GAN FALL]
I have no idea!

489
00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:37.350
Pierre! Don't worry about me!
You have to save the others!

490
00:28:37.430 --> 00:28:39.140
Pierre!

491
00:28:40.940 --> 00:28:43.400
[NAMI]
So what are we gonna
do now that the bird's gone,

492
00:28:43.470 --> 00:28:44.640
you weird old man?!

493
00:28:44.720 --> 00:28:46.850
[GAN FALL]
My name's Gan Fall.

494
00:28:46.930 --> 00:28:48.520
It's Gan Fall!

495
00:28:48.600 --> 00:28:51.190
[NAMI]
I don't care! Just save us!

496
00:28:51.270 --> 00:28:52.060
[whimpers]
